## Exercise 4 — two reasons to stop, told apart

Edit `ex4/solution.tsx`. Export a component.

```tsx
export function QuotePanel({
  symbol,
  timeoutMs,
  fetchQuote,
}: {
  symbol: string;
  timeoutMs: number;
  fetchQuote: (symbol: string, signal: AbortSignal) => Promise<string>;
}): JSX.Element;
```

The request must be given a signal that aborts when **either** of two things
happens: the component unmounts or `symbol` changes, or `timeoutMs`
milliseconds elapse. Compose them with `AbortSignal.any`.

Rendering:

- `<p role="status">Loading {symbol}</p>` while pending;
- the resolved string in a `<p>`;
- on timeout, `<p role="alert">Timed out loading {symbol}</p>`;
- on any other rejection, its message in `<p role="alert">`;
- on unmount or supersession, **nothing at all** — no state update, no alert.

The gate inspects the signal it was handed. After a `symbol` change it asserts
the abandoned signal is `aborted` and that its `reason` is an `AbortError`, not
a `TimeoutError`; it then advances fake timers past `timeoutMs` on the live
request and asserts the timeout alert appears rather than silence.

```
uv run dojo test react v3rb01_fetching_by_hand ex4
```

