## Hint 1

Two invariants are fighting here. "Append what arrives" wants to be a simple
`setItems(prev => [...prev, ...page.items])`. "Never append something from a
question I stopped asking" needs to know which question produced this page.
Give every page a stamp when it goes out, and check the stamp when it lands.

## Hint 2

A generation counter in a ref, bumped whenever the topic changes:

```tsx
const gen = useRef(0);
// on topic change: gen.current += 1; setItems([]); setCursor(null);
// when a page returns: if (myGen !== gen.current) return;
```

It is a ref rather than state because nothing renders it, and putting it in
state would put it in the effect's dependencies and start a loop.

## Hint 3

Deduplicating by id is one line if you build a `Set` of the ids you already
have and filter the incoming page against it. Do it in the updater function so
you are comparing against the *current* list rather than the one captured when
the request went out:

```tsx
setItems((prev) => {
  const seen = new Set(prev.map((i) => i.id));
  return [...prev, ...page.items.filter((i) => !seen.has(i.id))];
});
```

The double-click guard is the same `busy` flag that disables the button — but
check it in the handler too, because a disabled button can still be clicked
programmatically and because the flag is set asynchronously.

