## Challenge — a todo list that tells the truth

Edit `challenge/solution.tsx`. Assemble the sector.

```tsx
export type Todo = { clientId: string; serverId: string | null; title: string; done: boolean };

export function TodoApp({
  initial,
  api,
  newId,
}: {
  initial: Todo[];
  api: {
    create: (clientId: string, title: string) => Promise<{ id: string }>;
    toggle: (clientId: string, done: boolean) => Promise<{ done: boolean }>;
    remove: (clientId: string) => Promise<void>;
  };
  newId: () => string;
}): JSX.Element;
```

All of this at once:

1. **Add**: a form (`useActionState`) with an input named `title`. An empty
   title returns an error state without calling the API. Otherwise the row
   appears immediately with a client id, `serverId: null`, and
   `data-pending="true"`.
2. **Keys never change**: `clientId` is the React key for a row's whole life,
   and it is what `api.create` is called with.
3. **Toggle**: optimistic, using the layer model — a failed toggle reverts only
   that row, and a concurrent successful toggle of another row survives.
4. **Ordering**: two toggles of the *same* row, answered out of order, end in
   the state of the later click. Use a per-row version.
5. **Delete**: five-second undo window; `api.remove` is only called when the
   window closes; `Undo` restores position.
6. **Failures** are announced in a single `<div aria-live="polite">` region and
   the failed row is marked `data-failed="true"` with a `Retry` button that
   re-attempts that one mutation.
7. **No state update after unmount**, and every timer cleaned up.
8. Rows render as `<li>` with a checkbox labelled by the title and a
   `Delete {title}` button.

The gate walks all eight with fake timers and out-of-order resolution.

```
uv run dojo test react v3rb04_optimistic_updates challenge
```

